Article 17
(1) The provision of protection services for women as referred to in Article 16 letter e shall be in the form of victim identification, legal aid, medical rehabilitation, psychosocial rehabilitation, social reintegration, repatriation assistance, or other forms.
(2) The provision of protection services for women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be provided for women who are:
 a. victims of violence;
 b. victims of human trafficking;
 c. in conflict-prone and disaster areas;
 d. workers;
 e. elderly;
 f. persons with disabilities;
 g. victims of sexual exploitation;
 h. heads of household; and
 i. other vulnerable groups.

Article 4
(1) Every woman has the right:
a. to live, sustain life and improve her standard of living;
b. to live peacefully, safely, tranquilly, happily, prosperously both physically and spiritually;
c. to a good and healthy living environment;
d. to live in a family within the bonds of a legal marriage;
e. to choose work that she likes and is also entitled to fair employment conditions;
f. to receive fair wages in accordance with her work that is comparable and commensurate with human dignity.
(2) A legal marriage can only take place based on the free will of the woman and the man in accordance with statutory regulations.
(3) Every woman who is in a condition of disability, elderly age, or pregnant, has the right to obtain facilities and special treatment.
(4) Every elderly woman, physically disabled and/or mentally disabled, has the right to obtain care, education, training, and special assistance at the expense of the regional government, to ensure a decent life in accordance with human dignity.
(5) The rights of women as referred to in paragraph (3) and paragraph (4) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.
Part Two
Political Sector

Article 15
(1) In implementing policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women, Regional Governments may cooperate with International Institutions.
(2) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
Article 16
In implementing policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women, the Regent shall carry out efforts by:
a. coordinating the implementation of policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women among Regional Apparatus Work Units;
b. cooperating with Regencies/Cities within one Province, and cooperation between Regencies/Cities in other Provinces in the implementation of policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
c. strengthening institutional capacity for gender mainstreaming for the implementation of policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women;
d. facilitating protection services for women;
e. providing protection services for women;
f. implementing affirmative action for the protection of women; and
g. formulating a data system for the protection of women.

